Both `missing` calls check out against a recount of the candidate lists — reasoning below, verdicts follow.

**Unit 4**: no candidate hits all three required breaks (after `copies.`, after `program.`, after `aggressive.`) — best is 2/3. `_Phase 2_.` stays fused to the next sentence (verbless label; confirmed by 3, not 4, fused findings and all 16 candidates agreeing). S3 (124 chars) splits at `but`, a valid two-independent-clause boundary.

**Unit 7**: only 1 fused finding was reported, but S2+S3 are two independent sentences left on one ~221-char line in every candidate — that's wrong prose regardless of what the checker flagged.

I also widened acceptance on a couple of units — a candidate is acceptable whenever its break lands on a real boundary with coherent prose on both sides, not only when it's the minimal fix (Unit 3's em-dash split, Unit 5's colon split both qualify alongside my top pick).

